      "math_academy_id": "q-130044",
      "sequence_position": 19,
      "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{x+1},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,-2<y<0, \\\\ 3y\\sqrt{x},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<4,\\,-2<y<0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (-2,0)$ and ${R}_{2}=(1,4)\\times (-2,0).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}y{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}3y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}({e}^{x+1})(y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}(\\sqrt{x})(3y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y)+({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}3y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[{e}^{x+1}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-e)\\cdot (0-2)+(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot (0-6) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}+2e-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
